description:
Sets which edition the reader's current reading of a book is in: one of the book's known editions (edition_id, from list_book_editions), or the edition with an ISBN (isbn: 10 or 13 digits, as printed on the book or read from a photo of its barcode). An ISBN ReadingRate does not know yet is looked up in Open Library and added as an edition of the book, checked to be this book, and other readers can then pick it too; give translation_id (from list_book_editions) when you know whose translation it is. The reading's page count follows the edition unless the reader typed their own, and its cover follows unless they chose one. Earlier readings keep their own edition. clear: true clears the edition.
Use after list_book_editions, when the reader has said which edition they hold. To start a re-read first, use update_book_status with status "reading".
Examples:
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "edition_id": "<edition id>"}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "isbn": "9780679772835", "translation_id": "<translation id>"}
